mod DropPass

;; `keep` takes its argument owned and hands the same value back, so `"ok"` is
;; not freed when `keep` returns — `out` is about to read it. Only the value
;; `out` itself borrowed is freed, once: the position a call sits in says
;; nothing about what the callee does with its arguments.
keep (s:Str) : Str = s

main : E! Unit =
  out (keep "ok")
